{{ds:component/hero|title=Concepts|subtitle=The core building blocks every Godzilla pipeline is made of.|cta_html=<a href="{{cms:item/5ac66235-69dc-4092-b430-9d68837e0c76}}">Start with Pipelines</a>}}

<section>
  <p>Godzilla is built from core concepts that compose into everything else in these docs. Understanding how they relate makes the rest of the platform — guides, API reference, SDKs — much easier to follow.</p>

  {{ds:component/card|href={{cms:item/5ac66235-69dc-4092-b430-9d68837e0c76}}|tag=Concept|title=Pipelines|description=Named, versioned workflows that move data from a source to a destination through optional transforms.}}
  {{ds:component/card|href={{cms:item/7418c3d6-9ea1-4d1c-8d8f-73136f6b6abb}}|tag=Concept|title=Connectors|description=Pre-built integrations to external systems — sources, destinations, or both.}}
  {{ds:component/card|href={{cms:item/6277e4fb-3e99-45b0-a7f6-aefe69c5778f}}|tag=Concept|title=Events|description=The atomic unit of data flowing through a pipeline, plus the platform's own lifecycle events.}}
  {{ds:component/card|href={{cms:item/4d0a186a-d358-47c0-bd8f-26778f2732fe}}|tag=Concept|title=Schemas|description=Declarative contracts that define and validate the structure of event payloads flowing through pipelines.}}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>How they fit together</h2>
  <p>A <strong>pipeline</strong> reads <strong>events</strong> from a source <strong>connector</strong>, validates their <strong>schemas</strong>, transforms them, and writes them to a destination connector. Everything else in Godzilla — retries, webhooks, monitoring — is built on top of that single loop.</p>
</section>

